      "source": [
        "# Error Propagation in Physical Measurements\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overview\n",
        "This notebook explores **error propagation** - the study of how uncertainties in measured quantities affect the final result of calculations. When we measure physical quantities in experiments, no measurement is perfectly accurate. These small errors can accumulate and propagate through mathematical models, potentially affecting our conclusions."
      ]
