        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Case Study 1: Simple Harmonic Motion - Frequency Calculation\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🔬 Background & Theory\n",
        "\n",
        "**Simple Harmonic Motion (SHM)** is one of the most fundamental concepts in physics. When a mass is attached to a spring, it oscillates back and forth. The frequency of oscillation depends on two properties:\n",
        "- **Spring constant (k)**: How stiff the spring is (units: N/m)\n",
        "- **Mass (m)**: The mass attached to the spring (units: kg)\n",
        "\n",
        "The **angular frequency** is given by:\n",
        "$$\\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📊 The Problem\n",
        "\n",
        "In real experiments, we cannot measure $k$ and $m$ with perfect accuracy. If we have:\n",
        "- Uncertainty in spring constant: $\\Delta k = 20$ N/m\n",
        "- Uncertainty in mass: $\\Delta m = 0.2$ kg\n",
        "\n",
        "How much error does this introduce into our frequency calculation?\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📐 Error Propagation Formula\n",
        "\n",
        "For a function $f(k, m)$, we use **partial derivatives** to estimate the error:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\Delta f = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial k}\\Delta k\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial m}\\Delta m\\right)^2}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For our frequency formula:\n",
        "- $\\frac{\\partial \\omega}{\\partial k} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{km}}$\n",
        "- $\\frac{\\partial \\omega}{\\partial m} = -\\frac{\\sqrt{k}}{2m^{1.5}}$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ded29843-7dab-4471-a5a1-a2d03c4eeb5e",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "# Case 1: Spring-Mass System Frequency with Error Propagation\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Given measurements\nk = 1000  # Spring constant in N/m\ndk = 20   # Uncertainty in spring constant\n\nm = 10    # Mass in kg\ndm = 0.2  # Uncertainty in mass\n\n# Calculate the frequency\nf = np.sqrt(k/m)\n\n# Calculate error using partial derivatives\n# ∂ω/∂k = 1/(2√(km))\n# ∂ω/∂m = -√k/(2m^1.5)\nerr = np.sqrt(\n    (dk/(2*np.sqrt(k*m)))**2 +\n    ((np.sqrt(k)*dm)/(2*m**1.5))**2\n)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"CASE 1: Spring-Mass System\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(f\"Spring constant (k): {k} N/m ± {dk} N/m\")\nprint(f\"Mass (m): {m} kg ± {dm} kg\")\nprint(f\"\\nCalculated Angular Frequency: ω = {f:.4f} rad/s\")\nprint(f\"Error in frequency: Δω = {err:.6f} rad/s\")\nprint(f\"\\nRelative error: {(err/f)*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(\"\\n💡 Interpretation: A {:.2f}% uncertainty in measurements leads to a {:.2f}% error in frequency\".format(\n    ((dk/k)*100 + (dm/m)*100)/2, (err/f)*100\n))\n",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": "CASE 1: Spring-Mass System\n==================================================\nSpring constant (k): 1000 N/m ± 20 N/m\nMass (m): 10 kg ± 0.2 kg\n\nCalculated Angular Frequency: ω = 10.0000 rad/s\nError in frequency: Δω = 0.141421 rad/s\n",
          "text/plain": " RelativeError: 1.41%\n\n💡 Interpretation: A 1.10% uncertainty in measurements leads to a 1.41% error in frequency"
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 3
    },
