        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Case Study 2: Heat Transfer Through a Material\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🌡️ Background & Theory\n",
        "\n",
        "**Heat conduction** is the process by which thermal energy is transferred through a material. In thermal engineering, we often need to calculate the **heat flow rate** through a wall or material.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **Fourier heat conduction equation** tells us the heat transfer rate is:\n",
        "$$Q = \\frac{k \\cdot A \\cdot \\Delta T}{L}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:\n",
        "- **k** = Thermal conductivity (W/m·K)\n",
        "- **A** = Cross-sectional area (m²)\n",
        "- **ΔT** = Temperature difference (K)\n",
        "- **L** = Thickness of material (m)\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📊 The Problem\n",
        "\n",
        "We're designing an insulation system and have measured:\n",
        "- Thermal conductivity: k = 50 W/m·K with uncertainty ±1\n",
        "- Area: A = 0.5 m² with uncertainty ±0.01 m²\n",
        "- Temperature difference: ΔT = 100 K with uncertainty ±2 K\n",
        "- Thickness: L = 0.1 m with uncertainty ±0.002 m\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📐 Error Calculation\n",
        "\n",
        "For **multiple multiplicative/divisive terms**, we use **relative error propagation**:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\frac{\\Delta Q}{Q} = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\Delta k}{k}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\Delta A}{A}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\Delta T}{\\Delta T}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\Delta L}{L}\\right)^2}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This is useful because it shows which measurement is the **biggest source of uncertainty**!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "881e01e3-150d-4929-bac6-f1d4843bd8b7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "# Case 2: Heat Transfer with Multiple Parameters\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Measured parameters\nk = 50    # Thermal conductivity in W/m·K\nA = 0.5   # Area in m²\nt = 100   # Temperature difference in K\nL = 0.1   # Thickness in m\n\n# Measurement uncertainties\ndk = 1      # Uncertainty in k\ndA = 0.01   # Uncertainty in A\ndt = 2      # Uncertainty in t (temperature)\ndL = 0.002  # Uncertainty in L\n\n# Calculate heat transfer rate\nQ = k*A*t/L\n\n# Calculate relative error (using root sum of squares for relative errors)\nrel = np.sqrt(\n    (dk/k)**2 +\n    (dA/A)**2 +\n    (dt/t)**2 +\n    (dL/L)**2\n)\n\n# Absolute error\ndQ = Q*rel\n\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"CASE 2: Heat Transfer Through Material\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(f\"Thermal conductivity (k): {k} W/m·K ± {dk} W/m·K\")\nprint(f\"Cross-sectional area (A): {A} m² ± {dA} m²\")\nprint(f\"Temperature difference (ΔT): {t} K ± {dt} K\")\nprint(f\"Material thickness (L): {L} m ± {dL} m\")\nprint(f\"\\nCalculated Heat Flow Rate: Q = {Q:.1f} W\")\nprint(f\"Error in Q: ΔQ = ±{dQ:.1f} W\")\nprint(f\"\\nRelative error: {rel*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"\\n📊 Error Breakdown:\")\nprint(f\"  - From k uncertainty: {(dk/k)*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"  - From A uncertainty: {(dA/A)*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"  - From ΔT uncertainty: {(dt/t)*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"  - From L uncertainty: {(dL/L)*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"\\n💡 The largest contributor is: Temperature difference (±{(dt/t)*100:.2f}%)\")\n",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": "=CASE 2: Heat Transfer Through Material\n==================================================\nThermal conductivity (k): 50 W/m·K ± 1 W/m·K\nCross-sectional area (A): 0.5 m² ± 0.01 m²\nTemperature difference (ΔT): 100 K ± 2 K\nMaterial thickness (L): 0.1 m ± 0.002 m\n\nCalculated Heat Flow Rate: Q = 25000.0 W\nError in Q: ΔQ = ±1000.0 W\n",
          "text/plain": "Relative error: 4.00%\n\n📊 Error Breakdown:\n  - From k uncertainty: 2.00%\n  - From A uncertainty: 2.00%\n  - From ΔT uncertainty: 2.00%\n  - From L uncertainty: 2.00%\n\n💡 The largest contributor is: Temperature difference (±2.00%)"
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 5
    },
