        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Case Study 3: Reynolds Number - Fluid Flow Regime Detection\n",
        "\n",
        "### 💧 Background & Theory\n",
        "\n",
        "The **Reynolds number (Re)** is one of the most important dimensionless numbers in fluid mechanics. It tells us whether a fluid flow is **laminar** (smooth, ordered) or **turbulent** (chaotic, irregular).\n",
        "\n",
        "The Reynolds number is calculated as:\n",
        "$$Re = \\frac{\\rho \\cdot v \\cdot d}{\\mu}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:\n",
        "- **ρ (rho)** = Fluid density (kg/m³)\n",
        "- **v** = Velocity of the fluid (m/s)\n",
        "- **d** = Characteristic diameter (m)\n",
        "- **μ (mu)** = Dynamic viscosity (Pa·s)\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📊 The Problem\n",
        "\n",
        "We're studying fluid flow through a pipe and need to determine the flow regime. We've measured:\n",
        "- Density: ρ = 1000 kg/m³ with uncertainty ±20 kg/m³\n",
        "- Velocity: v = 2 m/s with uncertainty ±0.05 m/s\n",
        "- Diameter: d = 0.1 m with uncertainty ±0.002 m\n",
        "- Viscosity: μ = 0.001 Pa·s with uncertainty ±0.00002 Pa·s\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🎲 Monte Carlo Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of using calculus-based error propagation (which assumes small errors), we'll use **Monte Carlo simulation**:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Generate 100,000 random samples from each parameter's probability distribution\n",
        "2. Calculate Re for each combination\n",
        "3. Analyze the statistical distribution of results\n",
        "\n",
        "This approach is more accurate for **large errors** and **non-linear functions**!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d14702cf-c2a3-41cb-8516-26b06fb12b64",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "# Case 3: Reynolds Number Using Monte Carlo Simulation\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Set random seed for reproducibility\nnp.random.seed(42)\n\nn = 100000  # Number of simulations\n\n# Generate random samples from normal distributions (measurements with uncertainties)\nrho = np.random.normal(1000, 20, n)      # Density\nv = np.random.normal(2, 0.05, n)         # Velocity\nd = np.random.normal(0.1, 0.002, n)      # Diameter\nmu = np.random.normal(0.001, 0.00002, n) # Viscosity\n\n# Calculate Reynolds number for each sample\nRe = rho*v*d/mu\n\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"CASE 3: Reynolds Number - Flow Regime Analysis\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(f\"Number of Monte Carlo simulations: {n:,}\")\nprint(f\"\\nMeasured Parameters (mean ± std):\")\nprint(f\"  ρ (density): {np.mean(rho):.1f} ± {np.std(rho):.1f} kg/m³\")\nprint(f\"  v (velocity): {np.mean(v):.3f} ± {np.std(v):.4f} m/s\")\nprint(f\"  d (diameter): {np.mean(d):.4f} ± {np.std(d):.5f} m\")\nprint(f\"  μ (viscosity): {np.mean(mu):.6f} ± {np.std(mu):.8f} Pa·s\")\nprint(f\"\\nReynolds Number Results:\")\nprint(f\"  Mean Re: {np.mean(Re):.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  Std Dev: {np.std(Re):.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  Min Re: {np.min(Re):.2f}\")\nprint(f\"  Max Re: {np.max(Re):.2f}\")\nprint(f\"\\n🌊 Flow Regime Classification:\")\nlaminar = np.sum(Re < 2300)\ntransition = np.sum((Re >= 2300) & (Re <= 4000))\nturbulent = np.sum(Re > 4000)\nprint(f\"  Laminar (Re < 2300): {laminar:,} samples ({laminar/n*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"  Transition (2300 ≤ Re ≤ 4000): {transition:,} samples ({transition/n*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"  Turbulent (Re > 4000): {turbulent:,} samples ({turbulent/n*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"\\n⚠️  The flow regime is UNCERTAIN due to measurement errors!\")\n",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stdout",
          "text": "=================================================\nCASE 3: Reynolds Number - Flow Regime Analysis\n=================================================\nNumber of Monte Carlo simulations: 100,000\n\nMeasured Parameters (mean ± std):\n  ρ (density): 1000.2 ± 20.0 kg/m³\n  v (velocity): 2.000 ± 0.050 m/s\n  d (diameter): 0.1000 ± 0.0020 m\n  μ (viscosity): 0.0010 ± 0.0000 Pa·s\n\nReynolds Number Results:\n  Mean Re: 200053.79\n  Std Dev: 8576.31\n  Min Re: 163597.35\n  Max Re: 241625.44\n  \nFlow Regime Classification:\n  Laminar (Re < 2300): 0 samples (0.0%)\n  Transition (2300 ≤ Re ≤ 4000): 0 samples (0.0%)\n  Turbulent (Re > 4000): 100000 samples (100.0%)\n\n⚠️  The flow regime is UNCERTAIN due to measurement errors!"
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 6
